2. Write a Python program that calculates the variance and standard deviation of the 
dataset:6,7,8,9,10,11,12
Variance - It measures the average squared difference from the mean.
Standard Deviation - It’s simply the square root of variance.

import numpy as np
def main():
    values=[6,7,8,9,10,11,12]
    vari=np.var(values)
    std=np.std(values)
    print("Variance of above values:",vari)
    print("Standard Devition:",std)
